    description: "WHAT. Framework rows name a TYPE through base_class:, which reads the classes a symbol is an instance or subclass of, so they cannot fire and should not by that field. yesod.yaml: Handler, Widget, YForm/MForm/AForm, HandlerFor/HandlerT/HandlerM. servant.yaml: Handler, ServerT, ServerError, Application, Middleware, Request, Response. The Servant application row (base_class ^Application$, the ninth row of WI-dupis) is one of them: WAI's Application is a type synonym, and a Servant app is a binding declared \":: Application\" (app = serve api server). Also: yesod.yaml names YesodSubsite, which occurs nowhere in the yesod repository (YesodSubDispatch is the class).\n\nASK. haskell.py records no declared type a row could read (only Symbol.signature, which patterns must not read: ADR-0058). Proposal from the Haskell work, not built: write meta.return_type (the result type after the signature's last top-level arrow, forall and context stripped) and key the Servant row on meta_match return_type ^(IO )?Application$. return_type feeds signature_axis, so its consumers need auditing first, and whether a factory returning IO Application counts as an application is a decision. The other type-named rows: rekey or delete, row by row.\n\nFound during PR #2329 (2026-11-22). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/three_pr_plan_11222026/pr2/RESULTS.md and RESIDUALS_TO_FILE.md."  # 311b
    fields: {}  # 311b
